  "brief": "Bumble is being acquired by Ithaca Holdings in a $1.3 billion deal.\n\nIthaca Holdings / Bumble (Announced): Bumble Buyout by Ithaca Holdings. Bumble is being acquired by Ithaca Holdings in a $1.3 billion deal [1, 2, 3]. Bumble is in talks to go private with Ithaca Holdings [4, 5, 6].\nHorizon Space Acquisition I / ArcheNova Biotech (Announced): Horizon Space Acquisition I and ArcheNova Biotech Merger. Horizon Space Acquisition I and ArcheNova Biotech are merging [7, 8, 9]. The merger was announced on October 13 [7, 8, 9]. No further updates are available [10].\nSSR Mining / Roxmore Resources (Announced): SSR Mining to Acquire Roxmore Resources. SSR Mining is acquiring Roxmore Resources for $464 million [11, 12, 13]. The deal will expand SSR Mining's Nevada gold operations [11, 12, 13]. Roxmore Resources will spin out its exploration assets as part of the deal [11, 12, 13].\nAlbertsons / Kroger (Announced): Albertsons and Kroger Deal. Albertsons is demanding a large sum from Kroger over a failed merger [16, 17, 18]. The amount demanded is reportedly higher than initially stated [16, 17, 18]. The deal stands at the announced stage [14, 15, 20].\nOmron / OnLogic (Announced): Omron to Acquire OnLogic. Omron is acquiring OnLogic, a US industrial PC maker [21, 22, 23]. The deal is valued at $675 million [22]. The acquisition is part of Omron's physical AI push [21, 23].\nAslak / Al Raeda (Completed): Aslak and Al Raeda Deal. Aslak and Al Raeda have completed their deal [24, 25]. The deal was an acquisition of 40% of Al Raeda [24, 25].\nIonQ / Elisity (Announced): IonQ to Acquire Elisity. IonQ is acquiring Elisity in a $1.3 billion deal [28, 29, 30]. The deal is valued at up to $1.3 billion [26, 27, 31]. The acquisition is an all-stock deal [32]. The deal has been announced [26, 27, 28].\nAurum PropTech / Aurum RealEstate (Announced): Aurum PropTech Allocates Warrants to Promoter. Aurum PropTech has allotted ₹118 crore warrants to its promoter Aurum RealEstate [33]. The deal was announced on October 13 [33].\n\nAlso worth knowing:\n- Beam Global Signs Definitive Agreement to Acquire Drone Technology Company ScoutDI, Creating a Vertically Integrated U.S. Drone Platform for Industrial and Defense Markets [34].\n- Armstrong Bell acquires Tapcast in six-figure deal [35].\n- Morrisons sales rise faster than those at would-be bidder Sainsbury's for first time in five years amid signs of recovery [36].",
